Notebook[{Cell["HypergeometricK", "ObjectName"], 
  Cell["HypergeometricK[a, b, z] gives the inert generalized hypergeometric \
function with parameters a, b at K(z) = 1728/j.", "Usage"], 
  Cell["Status: Alpha.", "Notes"], Cell["HypergeometricK[a, b, z] gives the \
inert generalized hypergeometric function Sum_m Product (a)_m / Product (b)_m \
K^m / m! of K(z) = 1728/j(z), with exact parameter lists a and b (v1's FK).", 
   "Notes"], Cell["A denominator parameter that the series reaches as a \
nonpositive integer fails with SingularHypergeometric; a terminating series \
that stops first is accepted.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Options (shared configured settings can override these defaults):", 
   "Notes"], Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["Coordinate"], "TableText"], Cell["\"q\"", "TableText"], 
       Cell[
        "\"q\" (default) or \"tau\". Other values fail with InvalidOption.", 
        "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, 
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.02], Scaled[0.3], 
         Scaled[0.18], Scaled[0.5]}}]], "3ColumnTableMod"], 
